+The post-hoc E5 analysis asks whether the coefficient suggests a useful
+reference direction and magnitude for the real-data paired displacement.
+Using the training-objective quantities from Appendix~\ref{app:supp-real}, define
+\begin{equation}
+\label{eq:e5-proxy}
+p_{\gamma,H,m}
+=-\frac{\gamma^2}{m}\,\kappa(H)\,A_{\rm ref}^{-1}T_{\rm ref}[\Sigma_{\rm ref}],
+\qquad \kappa(H)=\frac{(H-1)(2H-1)}{12H}.
+\end{equation}
+This substitutes reference-point covariance $\Sigma_{\rm ref}/m$ into the
+additive-noise coefficient; no fitted scale is used. It is a proxy, not a
+proved expansion for state-dependent minibatch noise. The observed vector is
+$\widehat\Delta_K=R^{-1}\sum_r(Y_{r,K}^{\Scaf}-Y_{r,K}^{\FedAvg})$.
